  "description": "XESBUW crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H98 Dy8 N6 O32,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.598-4.012 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.09-116.26°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C76H100Dy8N8O32. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
